  "explanation": "The nasogastric tube tip should lie beyond the gastro-oesophageal junction, ideally within the stomach with side-port below the diaphragm. A tip positioned in the body of the stomach is generally acceptable, but if the radiograph shows malposition or the clinical context suggests concern, the statement may be false. In this imported item, the intended answer is that the tube is not in the normal position.",
